From: build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0028] venue study: three questions answered with real exchange data

Fetched from Bybit and Binance, frozen into bot/research/exchange_study/.
NOT under data/ — that holds CORPORA the book trades from, and
tests/test_market_data.py requires every file there to be in a MANIFEST. This is
a study set: fetched once, feeds no gate and no backtest. Filing it as a corpus
would claim a status it does not have.

1. THE VENUE MISMATCH IS NOT MATERIAL
Every corpus in this repo is Binance. CarryBroker places orders on Bybit. If
funding differed between venues by more than the edge, the entire backtest would
describe a trade nobody is going to make.

    4,431 matched funding prints
                     BYBIT   BINANCE
    mean bps         0.621     0.625
    stdev            1.031     0.859
    % positive       81.9      85.4
    annualised %     6.80      6.85
    difference                -0.04 %/yr

The OVERLAY decision holds on the venue that will actually trade. But BYBIT
FUNDING IS 20% NOISIER and positive less often — the same EWMA smoother sees a
wider distribution there, and the gate was tuned on the quieter one.

2. CAPACITY IS O($10-100M). NOT O($1bn), NOT O($1M).
"$100 is a ruler" has been in this repo since slice 1 with no number behind it.

    edge 214 bps per pair  (9.70%/yr x 3.98 yr / 18 trades, unfinanced)
    a round trip is FOUR legs: buy spot, sell perp, reverse both

    thinnest 1% band  $54M   (2024-08-05)
    deepest  1% band $244M   (2025-10-10)
    regime spread     4.6x

Trading the full 1% band costs ~200 bps of a 214 bps edge. So the book runs out
between $54M and $244M — and CAPACITY IS NOT A NUMBER, IT IS A NUMBER PER
REGIME. A size safe on a calm day is nearly 5x too large on a violent one.

STATED LIMIT, not hidden: bookDepth bands are 1% granularity, so impact BELOW
1% is unresolvable. Sizing between $100k and $10m needs L1/L2 tick data. The
tool says so rather than reporting a number the data cannot support.

3. THE HEDGE HOLDS UNDER STRESS — AND THIS IS THE LEVERAGE ARGUMENT

    day          price swing   basis range   basis sd
    2024-08-05        3.7%        5.3 bps      0.8
    2025-02-03        3.3%        5.6 bps      0.8
    2026-04-15        2.6%        6.3 bps      0.9

Price moved 260-370 bps. The basis moved 5-6. A hedged pair's P&L follows the
BASIS, not the price, so a day that would liquidate a 10x directional book moves
a 10x hedged book by roughly half a percent of equity.

That is the whole thesis, measured: 10x on a view is a countdown; 10x on this
spread is a different instrument. A test asserts the basis range stays under a
tenth of the price swing — if those were ever comparable, the hedge would not
be a hedge.

 + tools/venue_study.py          all three, read-only, feeds nothing
 + tests/test_venue_study.py     13 tests
 + research/exchange_study/      Bybit klines D+4h linear and spot, 4,600 Bybit
                                 funding prints, instrument rules, risk-limit
                                 ladder, 1m stress windows, and a median
                                 book-depth profile reduced from 2.9 MB of raw
                                 zips to 1.9 KB.

BORROW REMAINS UNMEASURED. Both public rate endpoints now 404 behind auth. It is
the single input that decides this business (+9.70% unfinanced vs -0.23% at 8%)
and it is specific to the operator, not to the market. It needs a quote, not a
